# Concept 1 — Mission Control (dense freeform grid)

Philosophy: dashboard = wall of instruments. Many small widgets, uniform
density, no hierarchy — the eye scans rows. Closest to status quo; pure
freeform RGL grid, composition is the user's job.

```
+--------+--------+--------+--------+--------+--------+
| METRIC | METRIC | METRIC | METRIC | METRIC | METRIC |
| Deals  | Won    | Value  | Vendors| Overdue| Members|
|  128   |  42    | $1.2M  |  57    |   7    |  14    |
+--------+--------+--------+--------+--------+--------+
| BREAKDOWN: deals by stage  | TREND: events 30d       |
|                            |                  .x     |
| open      ############ 64  |          .x. .x.x x.    |
| nego      ####### 38       |  x..x.x.x   x      x..x |
| won       ##### 26         |  ---------------------- |
+----------------------------+-------------------------+
| LIST: open deals (10)              | ATTENTION       |
| name         stage    amount       | COLD            |
| Acme Corp    open     $40k         |  o Initech      |
| Globex       nego     $25k         |  o Umbrella     |
| Hooli        open     $18k         | COOLING         |
| Initech      open     $12k         |  o Acme Corp    |
| ...                                |  o Stark Ind    |
+------------------------------------+-----------------+
| ACTIVITY: recent events across org                   |
| 10:42  anna   updated  Acme Corp     stage -> nego   |
| 10:31  jens   created  Vendor "Cloudly"              |
+------------------------------------------------------+
```

Composition rules: metric strip (h=1) pinned top; charts row middle;
heavy lists bottom. Everything optional, anything anywhere.

Best for: org-wide overview dashboards, exec "state of the world".
Risk: becomes a junk drawer; no guidance for what goes where.
